<div class="post-content">

  <p>
    Sewing machines turn cut parts into sewn assemblies. In soft-goods work, the right machine
    matters just as much as the right pattern, fabric, needle, and thread. A home machine and an
    industrial machine may both sew a straight seam, but they do not do it with the same speed,
    force, consistency, or range of features.
  </p>
  <p>
    In our studio context, the <strong>Juki 8700H</strong> and the <strong>Juki HZL-F600</strong>
    cover two very different roles. The 8700H is a focused production-style straight-stitch machine
    for longer seams and heavier work. The HZL-F600 is a flexible household machine that handles many
    stitch types, garment details, quilting tasks, and general prototyping.
  </p>

